 197:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/ssl_msg.c ****      *
 198:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/ssl_msg.c ****      * HMAC(msg) is defined as HASH(okey + HASH(ikey + msg)) where + means
 199:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/ssl_msg.c ****      * concatenation, and okey/ikey are the XOR of the key with some fixed bit
 200:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/ssl_msg.c ****      * patterns (see RFC 2104, sec. 2), which are stored in ctx->hmac_ctx.
 201:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/ssl_msg.c ****      *
 202:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/ssl_msg.c ****      * We'll first compute inner_hash = HASH(ikey + msg) by hashing up to
 203:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/ssl_msg.c ****      * minlen, then cloning the context, and for each byte up to maxlen
 204:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/ssl_msg.c ****      * finishing up the hash computation, keeping only the correct result.
 205:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/ssl_msg.c ****      *
 206:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/ssl_msg.c ****      * Then we only need to compute HASH(okey + inner_hash) and we're done.
