2131:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/ssl_msg.c ****  * Fill the input message buffer by appending data to it.
GAS LISTING /tmp/ccmtdssg.s 			page 90


2132:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/ssl_msg.c ****  * The amount of data already fetched is in ssl->in_left.
2133:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/ssl_msg.c ****  *
2134:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/ssl_msg.c ****  * If we return 0, is it guaranteed that (at least) nb_want bytes are
2135:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/ssl_msg.c ****  * available (from this read and/or a previous one). Otherwise, an error code
2136:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/ssl_msg.c ****  * is returned (possibly EOF or WANT_READ).
2137:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/ssl_msg.c ****  *
2138:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/ssl_msg.c ****  * With stream transport (TLS) on success ssl->in_left == nb_want, but
2139:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/ssl_msg.c ****  * with datagram transport (DTLS) on success ssl->in_left >= nb_want,
2140:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/ssl_msg.c ****  * since we always read a whole datagram at once.
2141:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/ssl_msg.c ****  *
2142:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/ssl_msg.c ****  * For DTLS, it is up to the caller to set ssl->next_record_offset when
2143:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/ssl_msg.c ****  * they're done reading a record.
2144:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/ssl_msg.c ****  */
