2171:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/ssl_msg.c ****         /*
2172:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/ssl_msg.c ****          * The point is, we need to always read a full datagram at once, so we
2173:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/ssl_msg.c ****          * sometimes read more then requested, and handle the additional data.
2174:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/ssl_msg.c ****          * It could be the rest of the current record (while fetching the
2175:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/ssl_msg.c ****          * header) and/or some other records in the same datagram.
