5869:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/ssl_msg.c ****             /* At this point, we don't know whether the renegotiation triggered
5870:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/ssl_msg.c ****              * by the post-handshake message has been completed or not. The cases
5871:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/ssl_msg.c ****              * to consider are the following:
5872:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/ssl_msg.c ****              * 1) The renegotiation is complete. In this case, no new record
5873:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/ssl_msg.c ****              *    has been read yet.
5874:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/ssl_msg.c ****              * 2) The renegotiation is incomplete because the client received
5875:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/ssl_msg.c ****              *    an application data record while awaiting the ServerHello.
5876:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/ssl_msg.c ****              * 3) The renegotiation is incomplete because the client received
5877:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/ssl_msg.c ****              *    a non-handshake, non-application data message while awaiting
5878:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/ssl_msg.c ****              *    the ServerHello.
5879:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/ssl_msg.c ****              *
5880:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/ssl_msg.c ****              * In each of these cases, looping will be the proper action:
5881:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/ssl_msg.c ****              * - For 1), the next iteration will read a new record and check
5882:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/ssl_msg.c ****              *   if it's application data.
5883:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/ssl_msg.c ****              * - For 2), the loop condition isn't satisfied as application data
5884:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/ssl_msg.c ****              *   is present, hence continue is the same as break
5885:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/ssl_msg.c ****              * - For 3), the loop condition is satisfied and read_record
5886:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/ssl_msg.c ****              *   will re-deliver the message that was held back by the client
5887:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/ssl_msg.c ****              *   when expecting the ServerHello.
5888:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/ssl_msg.c ****              */
